crau-nbd -- Linux Network Block Device server for CrAU v2 payload.bin

crau-nbd is a high-performance Linux Network Block Device (NBD) daemon
that maps and mounts partitions (read-only) inside ChromeOS and Android
OTA payload.bin images with zero intermediate disk extraction.

It strictly adheres to:
- IEEE Std 1003.1 (POSIX.1) Base Specifications
- GNU Coding Standards (https://www.gnu.org/prep/standards/standards.html)

For full documentation, refer to README.md or the manual page crau-nbd(1).
